# Pydantic Backend Rules

- Use Pydantic models for API inputs/outputs; avoid raw dictionaries at route boundaries.
- Prefer explicit field types and constraints (`Field`, enums, literals) over loose `Any`.
- Keep separate models for create/update/read flows when fields differ.
- Validate at boundaries (request parsing and config loading), not deep in business logic.
- Keep model names stable and semantic to preserve API contract clarity.

## Example
```python
class CreateLeadRequest(BaseModel):
    email: EmailStr
    source: Literal["web", "referral", "ads"]
```
